\title{BreedingR: Genetic Parameters, Breeding Values and Genomic Prediction}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Variance component estimation by AI-REML, breeding values, accuracy and single-step genomics (ssGBLUP), with reaction norms, direct-maternal and sire and maternal-grandsire models, several traits at once, metafounders, and a Gibbs sampler for Gaussian and binary traits. Single step also by the APY inverse or by markers as equations, with marker effects and quality control alongside. The numerics live in the package itself, in C++ with no external dependency, checked against independent paths: the dense V form, central finite differences, recovery of simulated components, and the published examples of Mrode and Pocrnic (2023). No package dependency at run time. Developed with support from the Sao Paulo Research Foundation (FAPESP), grants 2024/15502-6 and 2025/02949-5; the Coordenacao de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nivel Superior (CAPES), Finance Code 001; and the Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Cientifico e Tecnologico (CNPq).
